abstract: >-
  Quantum Mirror Theory reconceptualizes the observer-observed relationship 
  through the metaphor of reflection. Unlike prior interpretations that treat 
  measurement as collapse (Copenhagen), universe-splitting (Many-Worlds), or 
  hidden variable guidance (Pilot Wave), Mirror Theory proposes that observer 
  and observed are the SAME ENTITY viewed from different perspectives across 
  a "mirror boundary." We introduce the Mirror Equation |Ψ⟩ ≡ M|Ψ'⟩ and the 
  Mirror Constant 𝕄 as a measurable quantity for quantum coherence.
